{"availability":"available","full":"blain3white/next-fast-table","name":"next-fast-table","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":90,"forks":21,"created":"2024-07-19T14:35:02Z","updated":"2024-07-23T12:45:13Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://next-fast-table.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://next-fast-table.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:05.590Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:05.590Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:05.590Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T04:52:05.590Z","stars":90,"forks":21}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["🦄 NEXT-FAST-TABLE is an atomic, out-of-the-box frontend form component for backend management applications, based on Next.js.","NEXT-FAST-TABLE is a powerful and efficient table component designed for developers using Next.js. It simplifies the process of displaying complex data, allowing you to quickly create and integrate tables into your application within minutes.","As an independent developer, you can rapidly create a functional backend management framework similar to calling a library. It includes common CRUD operations and typical requirements like filtering and exporting. With NEXT-FAST-TABLE, you can focus more on core business logic rather than backend management. This tool enables independent developers, especially those using Next.js, to develop and deploy a functional backend management MVP in minutes rather than hours."],"features":["🔥 Easy to Use: Utilize Server Action for data handling without defining APIs explicitly. Alternatively, use fetch requests.","⭐️ Rich Presets: Easily generate forms by calling methods like Fields.string().","🔧 Highly Customizable: Supports various configuration options and style customization to meet diverse application needs.","📱 Responsive Design: Automatically adapts to various screen sizes, providing the best user experience.","⚙️ Advanced Data Handling: Built-in functionalities such as sorting, filtering, pagination, and fuzzy search for seamless integration."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/blain3white/next-fast-table/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"17dcd8a55e553e7c51916c4db452c26df445d7ad8eed047533866ef599c20447","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:05.733Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:05.733Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"🦄 NEXT-FAST-TABLE is an atomic, out-of-the-box frontend form component for backend management applications, based on Next.js.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/blain3white/next-fast-table/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"NEXT-FAST-TABLE is a powerful and efficient table component designed for developers using Next.js. It simplifies the process of displaying complex data, allowing you to quickly create and integrate tables into your application within minutes.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/blain3white/next-fast-table/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"17dcd8a55e553e7c51916c4db452c26df445d7ad8eed047533866ef599c20447","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/blain3white/next-fast-table/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:05.733Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2024-07-23T12:45:13Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/blain3white/next-fast-table/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:05.735Z","hash":"17dcd8a55e553e7c51916c4db452c26df445d7ad8eed047533866ef599c20447","originalBytes":15448,"storedBytes":15448,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["data","next-fast-table","const","function","developers","return","default","backend","used","export","type","async","column","example","only","payment","project","sorting","component","create","development","false","install","many","next.js","string","table","using","when","application","bash","complete","define","description","need","npm","options","returns","whether","any","await","columns","configurati